## End-to-End Tests

- `apps/e2e` holds the Playwright specs (`specs/*.spec.ts`) and the stack they run against. Specs drive the app like a user: roles, labels and visible text, never implementation details; each one creates the data it needs (a fresh account per run) so it passes on a reused stack too.
- `pnpm run e2e` boots this checkout's stack, runs every spec and removes the stack. The stack runs the dev setup in its own slot: its own compose project with fresh containers of the dev services, its own data folder, and every app on its own ports (each dev port plus 10000, plus the slot number). The environment is `.env.example` with those ports and the `data/` folder moved, so a running `pnpm run dev` or another checkout's stack never collides with it.
- The stack serves the web app from a production build (`build`, then `serve`) so pages load like the deployed app; other apps run their `dev` script. A web change shows in the specs once the stack restarts.
- Run specs repeatedly against one stack: `pnpm run e2e:stack` in one terminal, then `E2E_REUSE_STACK=true pnpm run e2e specs/<file>.spec.ts`; `pnpm run e2e:cleanup` stops the stack and removes its containers. `pnpm run e2e:preflight` checks Docker, the browser and the slot's ports when a boot fails. `E2E_STACK_SLOT=<n>` pins a slot.
- On start the stack applies the database migrations (`db:migrate`); commit them (`pnpm run db:generate`). Shared seed data goes in `apps/e2e/src/data/stack-seeds.ts` and must be idempotent.
- CI runs the specs in an `e2e` job of its own; the HTML report and traces of a failed run are uploaded as the `playwright-report` artifact.
- Record UI demos for pull requests with `pnpm run e2e:record`; see the `pr-demo-proof` skill.
